{"type":"Film","id":"FR2014_128","slug":"fr2014-128-breves-de-comptoir","title":{"native":"Brèves de comptoir","english":""},"release":{"type":"Theatrical release","date":"2014-09-24","year":2014},"filmType":"Fiction film","directors":[{"id":"Jean-Michel Ribes","slug":"jean-michel-ribes","name":"Jean-Michel Ribes","birthYear":1946,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[]}],"genre":["Comedy","Multi-protagonist film"],"media":{"posterUrl":"https://medias.unifrance.org/medias/51/243/127795/format_page/breves-de-comptoir.jpg","trailerUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SLMclo_eu-k"},"synopsis":{"native":"Une journée de la vie du Café L’Hirondelle, sur une petite place de banlieue, en face d’un cimetière. De l’ouverture à 6h30 du matin jusqu’à la fermeture à 22h30, les clients entrent, boivent, parlent, sortent, rerentrent, re-boivent et reparlent de plus belle. Ils composent un drôle d’opéra parlé, une musique tendre et cocasse, un cantique de pensées frappées au coin du plaisir d’être ensemble, un verre de vin blanc à la main. Le génie populaire danse.","english":"A day at L’Hirondelle café, in a small suburban square, opposite the cemetery. Right from when it opens at 6.30am until it closes at 10.30pm, clients come in, drink, talk, go out, come back, drink and talk some more. They create a curious spoken opera, soft and comical music, a hymn of wild thoughts produced from the pleasure of being together, a glass of white wine in hand."},"production":[{"country":"France","share":"Majority coproducer"}],"characters":[{"id":"FR2014_128_01","film":"FR2014_128","person":{"id":"Chantal Neuwirth","slug":"chantal-neuwirth","name":"Chantal Neuwirth","birthYear":1948,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Female identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[]},"age":"2: Late Middle Age (55-60)","gender":"Female identifying","sexuality":"Heterosexual","origin":"White Western European","class":"Middle class","profession":"Self-employed","ability":"Able-bodie